# Home Assistant specification coverage

Home Assistant already provides device controls, automation editors, schedules, history, account management and recovery flows. The gaps below concern **civica.uk design specifications and acceptance coverage** for those capabilities. They are not a claim that Home Assistant lacks the features.

The review identified 30 areas needing a dedicated specification or a more complete task contract. Each now has a linked guide with state/capability decisions, complete examples, accessibility and recovery guidance, and integration acceptance recipes. Start with the [Home Assistant catalogue](../home-assistant/index.html). Completion means design coverage; it does not mean a new native adapter or live device test.

