## Review and implementation limits

The specifications are reviewed against the frozen [brand guidance](../styles/brand-colour.html) and [writing guide](../content/index.html). Their rules preserve native labels, user names, translations, permissions, data values and device capabilities. Illustration rules do not justify replacing functional icons, camera images or maps. A clinical or government source does not give this household application its authority or assurance.

The source review established the original gaps. The implementation adds dedicated guides and examples, checked by the build and browser suite described in the [work package](guidance-work-package.html). Those checks use synthetic data; they do not operate household devices or certify complete native task accessibility. The [whole-system audit](design-system-audit.html) keeps confirmed implementation findings separate from this specification coverage register. Use the [audit checklist](../reference/component-audit-checklist.json) to repeat the review when the sources, rules or implementation change.
